# TreeTagger Persian tagset
#
# Persian TreeTagger Part-of-Speech Tags. The coarse part-of-speech is encoded in the
# head of each tag (the part before the first '.') and follows the Universal POS
# categories (ADJ, ADP, ADV, AUX, CCONJ, DET, INTJ, NOUN, NUM, PART, PRON, PROPN,
# PUNCT, SCONJ, VERB, X); the remainder encodes morphological features. Portmanteau
# tags (joined with '+', e.g. ADP+PRON, ADJ+AUX, an enclitic '+PUNCT') are mapped by
# their first/main component. Standalone punctuation tokens (" « » ( ) : ) and SENT
# are mapped to POS_PUNCT. This is distinct from the fa-upc tagset (fa-upc-pos.map).
#
# Source: extracted from the TreeTagger model using TT4J
